; Program 5.30: Roots of a2 x² + a1 x + a0 = 0 with a smaller error for real roots:
;   the larger root x1 by the usual formula, the smaller one as x2 = a0/(a2·x1)
; Source: Дьяконов, «Справочник по расчётам на микрокалькуляторах», 1985, p.97-98 (book61.pdf pages 98-99)
; Input: a0 in Rc, a1 in Rb, a2 in Ra; В/О, С/П.
; Output: real roots: 7 in X, x1 in R7, x2 in R8;
;   complex roots x1,2 = d ± j·m: 4 in X, d in R4, m in R5.
; (The book's text writes x2 = −a0/(x1·a2); the program computes a0/(a2·x1), the
; correct Vieta product; step 27 is the "+"-like glyph read as ÷.)
;
; Book example: 3x² + 20000x + 12 = 0 -> x1 = −6666,666, x2 = −6,0000006·10^-4
; (program 5.29 gives x2 = −6,6666666·10^-4 here; exact 6·10^-4)
; @reg Rc=12 Rb=20000 Ra=3
; @run
; @expect X=7
; @expect R7=-6666.666
; @expect R8=-6.0000006e-4
; @reset
; Complex case: the book's 5.29 example x² + 2x + 15 = 0 -> −1 ± j·3,7416573
; (expected value computed, not printed in the book for this program)
; @reg Rc=15 Rb=2 Ra=1
; @run
; @expect X=4
; @expect R4=-1
; @expect R5=3.7416573
;
00: ИПc ИПa ÷ П9 ИПb /-/ ИПa 2 × ÷
10: П4 Fx² − Fx<0 31 /-/ F√ ИП4 Fx<0 23
20: ↔ − 0 + П7 ИП9 ↔ ÷ П8 7
30: С/П F√ П5 4 С/П
